  "hindi": "उस तुम दोनों के रथ को, जो दूर तक दौड़ने वाला है, गौ का मिलन है, हे अश्विनो, हम आज बुलाएँ — जो आसन वाला होकर सूर्या को वहन करता है; स्तुति को वहन करने वाला, सबसे अधिक, धन चाहने वाला।",
  "english": "That chariot of you two, wide-coursing, the meeting of the cow, O Aśvins, may we invoke today — which, having a seat, carries Sūryā; hymn-carrying, most abundant, desiring wealth.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Several words are unclear. vandhurāyuḥ is translated 'having a seat' (vandhura 'chariot seat' + -āyu; form and sense uncertain). saṃgatiṃ goḥ translated literally 'the meeting of the cow'. girvāhasam read as 'hymn-carrying'. huvema read as 1 pl. optative. Accusatives girvāhasam, purutamam, vasūyum agree with ratham.",
  "confidence": "low"
